ccamlr_statistical_areas.geojson
--------------------------------

CCAMLR statistical areas, Commission for the Conservation of Antarctic
Marine Living Resources (CCAMLR GIS, https://gis.ccamlr.org).

The subareas and divisions of Areas 48, 58 and 88: 19 Polygon features in
EPSG:6932 (WGS 84 / NSIDC EASE-Grid 2.0 South), written by GDAL as GeoJSON
with a "crs" member (not RFC 7946 lon/lat), coordinates in metres rounded
to the metre. Six attributes, the ones used as popups: GAR_ID, GAR_Name,
GAR_Short_Label, GAR_Long_Label, GAR_Start_Date and GAR_Size.

Simplified for size (about 92 KB, from 38,112 vertices to 4,817): each
polygon on its own, with sf::st_simplify(preserveTopology = TRUE,
dTolerance = 2000), a 2 km tolerance. Because each polygon is simplified
separately, the shared edges of neighbouring areas no longer match
exactly: there are small gaps and overlaps along them.

This copy is illustrative, for examples and tests. It is not an
authoritative statement of the boundaries; use the data from CCAMLR GIS
for that.

Made 2026-10-01 by tools/make-ccamlr-fixture.R (in the source repository,
not the installed package) from a GeoParquet copy of the CCAMLR
statistical areas layer.
